  "Committed result of spikes/renderer/tools/surface-lock-audit.py, which counts every",
  "SurfaceClass::Lock caller and separates the ones outside the 19 files that contain a",
  "direct D3D8 lock call.  `stores`/`loads` are mechanical: a load is any use of the",
  "returned pointer that is not a store through it, so null checks and pass-to-callee",
  "count as loads and the number is an upper bound on real texel reads.",
  "`gpu_provenance` means the locked surface can hold pixels the GPU wrote (a back",
  "buffer or render target copied in with _Copy_DX8_Rects); load + gpu_provenance is the",
  "hazard renderer-resource-seam.md 7.1 describes.  --check fails if these counts move,",
  "so a new SurfaceClass::Lock caller forces a class decision."
